# Task: Implement Vectored I/O Support

## What

Add scatter/gather I/O (readv/writev) support to TcpStream, UnixStream for efficient multi-buffer operations.

## Why

Vectored I/O allows reading/writing multiple non-contiguous buffers in a single syscall:
- Efficient protocol framing (header + body)
- Zero-copy when possible
- Reduced syscall overhead

## Design

### AsyncRead Extension

```rust
/// Extension trait for vectored reading.
pub trait AsyncReadVectored: AsyncRead {
    fn poll_read_vectored(
        self: Pin<&mut Self>,
        cx: &mut Context<'_>,
        bufs: &mut [IoSliceMut<'_>],
    ) -> Poll<io::Result<usize>>;
}

// Convenience method
pub trait AsyncReadVectoredExt: AsyncReadVectored {
    async fn read_vectored(&mut self, bufs: &mut [IoSliceMut<'_>]) -> io::Result<usize> {
        poll_fn(|cx| Pin::new(&mut *self).poll_read_vectored(cx, bufs)).await
    }
}
```

### AsyncWrite Extension

```rust
/// Extension trait for vectored writing.
pub trait AsyncWriteVectored: AsyncWrite {
    fn poll_write_vectored(
        self: Pin<&mut Self>,
        cx: &mut Context<'_>,
        bufs: &[IoSlice<'_>],
    ) -> Poll<io::Result<usize>>;

    /// Check if implementation supports vectored writes efficiently.
    fn is_write_vectored(&self) -> bool {
        false // Default: no efficient support
    }
}
```

### Implementation for TcpStream

```rust
impl AsyncReadVectored for TcpStream {
    fn poll_read_vectored(
        self: Pin<&mut Self>,
        cx: &mut Context<'_>,
        bufs: &mut [IoSliceMut<'_>],
    ) -> Poll<io::Result<usize>> {
        match self.inner.read_vectored(bufs) {
            Ok(n) => Poll::Ready(Ok(n)),
            Err(ref e) if e.kind() == io::ErrorKind::WouldBlock => Poll::Pending,
            Err(e) => Poll::Ready(Err(e)),
        }
    }
}

impl AsyncWriteVectored for TcpStream {
    fn poll_write_vectored(
        self: Pin<&mut Self>,
        cx: &mut Context<'_>,
        bufs: &[IoSlice<'_>],
    ) -> Poll<io::Result<usize>> {
        match self.inner.write_vectored(bufs) {
            Ok(n) => Poll::Ready(Ok(n)),
            Err(ref e) if e.kind() == io::ErrorKind::WouldBlock => Poll::Pending,
            Err(e) => Poll::Ready(Err(e)),
        }
    }

    fn is_write_vectored(&self) -> bool {
        true // TcpStream supports efficient vectored writes
    }
}
```

