# RaptorQ Decoding Pipeline

## Overview
Implements the core RaptorQ fountain code decoding pipeline that reconstructs original data from a set of received symbols, tolerating symbol loss and corruption.

## Technical Background

RaptorQ decoding reconstructs K source symbols from:
- Any K' symbols where K' is slightly larger than K (typically K' = K * 1.01 + 2)
- Mix of source and repair symbols
- Symbols can arrive out of order

The key insight: decode succeeds probabilistically once threshold is met.

## Architecture

```
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|                    DecodingPipeline                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|  Input: Stream of (SymbolId, Symbol) pairs                |
|                  |                                         |
|  +-----------------------------------+                     |
|  | 1. Symbol Collection              |                     |
|  |    - Track received symbols       |                     |
|  |    - Deduplicate by SymbolId      |                     |
|  |    - Group by Source Block Number |                     |
|  +-----------------------------------+                     |
|                  |                                         |
|  +-----------------------------------+                     |
|  | 2. Threshold Detection            |                     |
|  |    - Monitor per-block counts     |                     |
|  |    - Trigger decode at K'         |                     |
|  +-----------------------------------+                     |
|                  |                                         |
|  +-----------------------------------+                     |
|  | 3. Matrix Inversion               |                     |
|  |    - Build encoding matrix        |                     |
|  |    - Gaussian elimination         |                     |
|  |    - Back-substitution            |                     |
|  +-----------------------------------+                     |
|                  |                                         |
|  +-----------------------------------+                     |
|  | 4. Source Symbol Recovery         |                     |
|  |    - Compute intermediate symbols |                     |
|  |    - Generate missing source      |                     |
|  |    - Verify via authentication    |                     |
|  +-----------------------------------+                     |
|                  |                                         |
|  Output: Result<Vec<u8>, DecodingError>                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
```

## Core Types

