# Bug Fix: HPACK Integer Overflow (COMPLETED)

## Status: FIXED in session 2026-01-31

## Location
`src/http/h2/hpack.rs` - decode_integer function

## Vulnerability
The shift amount was checked AFTER the addition, allowing overflow on malformed input.
An attacker could craft input causing integer overflow leading to incorrect decoding
or potential memory corruption.

## Original Code
```rust
loop {
    let byte = *bytes.get(pos).ok_or_else(|| H2Error::compression("truncated"))?;
    pos += 1;
    value += ((byte & 0x7f) as usize) << shift;  // Overflow before check!
    if shift > 28 {
        return Err(H2Error::compression("integer too large"));
    }
    // ...
}
```

## Fix Applied
Check shift BEFORE addition, use checked arithmetic:

```rust
loop {
    let byte = *bytes.get(pos).ok_or_else(|| H2Error::compression("truncated"))?;
    pos += 1;

    // Check shift limit BEFORE the addition
    if shift > 28 {
        return Err(H2Error::compression("integer too large"));
    }

    let increment = ((byte & 0x7f) as usize)
        .checked_shl(shift)
        .ok_or_else(|| H2Error::compression("integer overflow in shift"))?;

    value = value
        .checked_add(increment)
        .ok_or_else(|| H2Error::compression("integer overflow in addition"))?;

    // ...
}
```

