# no_ambient_authority Test Oracle

## Purpose
Verify the 6th non-negotiable invariant: "No ambient authority - effects flow through Cx and explicit capabilities."

This oracle detects violations where code performs effects (I/O, spawning, timing, etc.) without going through the explicit capability system.

## Invariant Definition

**No Ambient Authority**: All observable effects in the system must be traceable to explicit capability grants through the `Cx` context. Tasks cannot:
- Spawn other tasks without `Cx::spawn`
- Access time without `Cx::now` or `Cx::sleep`
- Perform I/O without I/O capabilities
- Access global state without explicit grants

## Oracle Implementation

### Capability Tracking
```rust
/// Tracks all capability usage during execution
pub struct CapabilityTracker {
    /// Effects performed, keyed by task
    effects: HashMap<TaskId, Vec<Effect>>,
    /// Capability grants, keyed by task
    grants: HashMap<TaskId, CapabilitySet>,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone)]
pub enum Effect {
    Spawn { child: TaskId },
    Sleep { duration: Duration },
    TimeAccess,
    ChannelSend { channel_id: ChannelId },
    ChannelRecv { channel_id: ChannelId },
    Trace { message: String },
    RegionCreate { region_id: RegionId },
    ObligationCreate { obligation_id: ObligationId },
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Default)]
pub struct CapabilitySet {
    can_spawn: bool,
    can_time: bool,
    can_trace: bool,
    channel_access: HashSet<ChannelId>,
    region_access: HashSet<RegionId>,
}
```

### Verification Logic
```rust
impl CapabilityTracker {
    /// Verify no ambient authority violations
    pub fn verify(&self) -> Result<(), AmbientAuthorityViolation> {
        for (task_id, effects) in &self.effects {
            let grants = self.grants.get(task_id)
                .ok_or(AmbientAuthorityViolation::NoCapabilityContext { task_id: *task_id })?;

            for effect in effects {
                self.verify_effect(*task_id, effect, grants)?;
            }
        }
        Ok(())
    }

    fn verify_effect(
        &self,
        task_id: TaskId,
        effect: &Effect,
        grants: &CapabilitySet,
    ) -> Result<(), AmbientAuthorityViolation> {
        match effect {
            Effect::Spawn { child } => {
                if !grants.can_spawn {
                    return Err(AmbientAuthorityViolation::UnauthorizedSpawn {
                        task_id,
                        child: *child,
                    });
                }
            }
            Effect::Sleep { .. } | Effect::TimeAccess => {
                if !grants.can_time {
                    return Err(AmbientAuthorityViolation::UnauthorizedTimeAccess {
                        task_id,
                    });
                }
            }
            Effect::ChannelSend { channel_id } | Effect::ChannelRecv { channel_id } => {
                if !grants.channel_access.contains(channel_id) {
                    return Err(AmbientAuthorityViolation::UnauthorizedChannelAccess {
                        task_id,
                        channel_id: *channel_id,
                    });
                }
            }
            Effect::Trace { .. } => {
                if !grants.can_trace {
                    return Err(AmbientAuthorityViolation::UnauthorizedTrace {
                        task_id,
                    });
                }
            }
            Effect::RegionCreate { region_id } => {
                // Must have parent region access
                if !grants.region_access.iter().any(|r| self.is_ancestor(*r, *region_id)) {
                    return Err(AmbientAuthorityViolation::UnauthorizedRegionCreate {
                        task_id,
                        region_id: *region_id,
                    });
                }
            }
            Effect::ObligationCreate { .. } => {
                // Obligations are tied to channel/resource access
                // Verified through the specific resource
            }
        }
        Ok(())
    }
}
```

### Error Types
```rust
#[derive(Debug, Error)]
pub enum AmbientAuthorityViolation {
    #[error("Task {task_id:?} has no capability context")]
    NoCapabilityContext { task_id: TaskId },

    #[error("Task {task_id:?} spawned {child:?} without spawn capability")]
    UnauthorizedSpawn { task_id: TaskId, child: TaskId },

    #[error("Task {task_id:?} accessed time without time capability")]
    UnauthorizedTimeAccess { task_id: TaskId },

    #[error("Task {task_id:?} accessed channel {channel_id:?} without capability")]
    UnauthorizedChannelAccess { task_id: TaskId, channel_id: ChannelId },

    #[error("Task {task_id:?} traced without trace capability")]
    UnauthorizedTrace { task_id: TaskId },

    #[error("Task {task_id:?} created region {region_id:?} without parent access")]
    UnauthorizedRegionCreate { task_id: TaskId, region_id: RegionId },
}
```

