# Task: Implement UnixListener with Reactor Integration

## What

Create UnixListener type for accepting Unix domain socket connections, integrated with the reactor.

## Location

`src/net/unix/listener.rs` (new file)
`src/net/unix/mod.rs` (new module)

## Design

```rust
use std::os::unix::net::{self, SocketAddr};
use std::path::Path;

/// A Unix domain socket listener.
pub struct UnixListener {
    inner: net::UnixListener,
    registration: Option<Registration>,
    path: Option<PathBuf>, // For cleanup on drop
}

impl UnixListener {
    /// Bind to a filesystem path.
    ///
    /// The socket file is created at the specified path. It will be
    /// removed when the listener is dropped.
    pub async fn bind<P: AsRef<Path>>(path: P) -> io::Result<Self> {
        let path = path.as_ref();

        // Remove existing socket file if present
        let _ = std::fs::remove_file(path);

        let inner = net::UnixListener::bind(path)?;
        inner.set_nonblocking(true)?;

        // Register with reactor
        let cx = Cx::current();
        let registration = cx.register_io(
            &UnixListenerSource(&inner),
            Interest::READABLE,
        )?;

        Ok(Self {
            inner,
            registration: Some(registration),
            path: Some(path.to_path_buf()),
        })
    }

    /// Bind to an abstract namespace socket (Linux only).
    #[cfg(target_os = "linux")]
    pub async fn bind_abstract(name: &[u8]) -> io::Result<Self> {
        use std::os::linux::net::SocketAddrExt;

        let addr = SocketAddr::from_abstract_name(name)?;
        let inner = net::UnixListener::bind_addr(&addr)?;
        inner.set_nonblocking(true)?;

        let cx = Cx::current();
        let registration = cx.register_io(
            &UnixListenerSource(&inner),
            Interest::READABLE,
        )?;

        Ok(Self {
            inner,
            registration: Some(registration),
            path: None, // No filesystem path for abstract sockets
        })
    }

    /// Accept a new connection.
    pub async fn accept(&self) -> io::Result<(UnixStream, SocketAddr)> {
        poll_fn(|cx| self.poll_accept(cx)).await
    }

    /// Poll for a new connection.
    pub fn poll_accept(&self, cx: &mut Context<'_>) -> Poll<io::Result<(UnixStream, SocketAddr)>> {
        match self.inner.accept() {
            Ok((stream, addr)) => {
                stream.set_nonblocking(true)?;

                // Create UnixStream with registration
                let cx_runtime = Cx::current();
                let registration = cx_runtime.register_io(
                    &UnixStreamSource(&stream),
                    Interest::READABLE | Interest::WRITABLE,
                )?;

                let unix_stream = UnixStream {
                    inner: stream,
                    registration: Some(registration),
                };

                Poll::Ready(Ok((unix_stream, addr)))
            }
            Err(ref e) if e.kind() == io::ErrorKind::WouldBlock => {
                // Reactor will wake when connection pending
                Poll::Pending
            }
            Err(e) => Poll::Ready(Err(e)),
        }
    }

    /// Get the local socket address.
    pub fn local_addr(&self) -> io::Result<SocketAddr> {
        self.inner.local_addr()
    }

    /// Create from standard library type.
    pub fn from_std(listener: net::UnixListener) -> io::Result<Self> {
        listener.set_nonblocking(true)?;

        let cx = Cx::current();
        let registration = cx.register_io(
            &UnixListenerSource(&listener),
            Interest::READABLE,
        )?;

        Ok(Self {
            inner: listener,
            registration: Some(registration),
            path: None, // Don't know the path
        })
    }
}

impl Drop for UnixListener {
    fn drop(&mut self) {
        // Clean up socket file
        if let Some(path) = &self.path {
            let _ = std::fs::remove_file(path);
        }
        // Registration dropped automatically (RAII)
    }
}

// Source trait impl for reactor registration
struct UnixListenerSource<'a>(&'a net::UnixListener);

impl<'a> Source for UnixListenerSource<'a> {
    fn raw_fd(&self) -> RawFd {
        self.0.as_raw_fd()
    }

    fn source_id(&self) -> u64 {
        // Use a unique counter
        static COUNTER: AtomicU64 = AtomicU64::new(0);
        COUNTER.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed)
    }
}
```

## Socket File Cleanup

Important: Unix socket files persist after process exit. We must clean up:
1. Before bind: Remove existing file (might be stale)
2. On drop: Remove our socket file

## Abstract Namespace (Linux)

Linux supports abstract namespace sockets:
- Start with null byte `\0`
- Not bound to filesystem
- Automatically cleaned up by kernel
- No permission issues

