# 0.1: Cx Capability Token Public API

## Objective
Make the Cx (capability context) type fully usable by external crates like fastapi_rust.

## Background

### What is Cx?
Cx is Asupersync's capability boundary - all effectful operations (spawn, sleep, I/O, trace) flow through explicit Cx tokens. This prevents ambient authority and enables:
- Effect interception (production vs lab runtime)
- Cancellation propagation
- Budget enforcement
- Tracing/observability

### Why fastapi_rust Needs Cx
RequestContext will wrap Cx to provide HTTP-specific context:
```rust
pub struct RequestContext<'a> {
    cx: Cx<'a>,           // ALL async capabilities come from here
    request: &'a Request,
    // ...
}

impl<'a> RequestContext<'a> {
    pub fn spawn<F>(&self, f: F) -> JoinHandle<F::Output>
    where F: Future + Send + 'static {
        self.cx.spawn(f)  // Delegate to Cx
    }

    pub fn check_cancelled(&self) -> bool {
        self.cx.is_cancel_requested()
    }
}
```

