# 0.1: Cx Capability Token Public API

## Objective
Make the Cx (capability context) type fully usable by external crates like fastapi_rust.

## Background

### What is Cx?
Cx is Asupersync's capability boundary - all effectful operations (spawn, sleep, I/O, trace) flow through explicit Cx tokens. This prevents ambient authority and enables:
- Effect interception (production vs lab runtime)
- Cancellation propagation
- Budget enforcement
- Tracing/observability

### Why fastapi_rust Needs Cx
RequestContext will wrap Cx to provide HTTP-specific context:
```rust
pub struct RequestContext<'a> {
    cx: Cx<'a>,           // ALL async capabilities come from here
    request: &'a Request,
    // ...
}

impl<'a> RequestContext<'a> {
    pub fn spawn<F>(&self, f: F) -> JoinHandle<F::Output>
    where F: Future + Send + 'static {
        self.cx.spawn(f)  // Delegate to Cx
    }

    pub fn check_cancelled(&self) -> bool {
        self.cx.is_cancel_requested()
    }
}
```

## Requirements

### 1. Visibility
- [ ] `Cx` struct is `pub` in lib.rs re-exports
- [ ] All methods fastapi_rust needs are `pub`
- [ ] `CxRef` or similar for borrowed context patterns

### 2. Documentation
- [ ] Module-level doc explaining capability model
- [ ] Each public method has doc comment with example
- [ ] "Wrapping Cx" section for framework authors
- [ ] Lifetime requirements clearly documented

### 3. API Surface
Methods that MUST be public for fastapi_rust:
```rust
impl<'a> Cx<'a> {
    // Spawning (for background tasks in handlers)
    pub fn spawn<F>(&self, f: F) -> JoinHandle<F::Output>;

    // Timing (for timeouts, delays)
    pub fn sleep(&self, duration: Duration) -> Sleep;
    pub fn sleep_until(&self, deadline: Instant) -> Sleep;
    pub fn deadline(&self) -> Option<Instant>;

    // Cancellation (for graceful shutdown)
    pub fn is_cancel_requested(&self) -> bool;
    pub fn cancel_token(&self) -> CancelToken;

    // Budget (for request timeouts)
    pub fn remaining_budget(&self) -> Budget;
    pub fn with_budget(&self, budget: Budget) -> Cx<'_>;

    // Observability (for request tracing)
    pub fn trace(&self, level: Level, message: &str);
    pub fn span(&self, name: &str) -> Span;

    // Region (for structured concurrency)
    pub fn region<F>(&self, f: F) -> RegionFuture<F::Output>;
}
```

### 4. Extension Pattern
Document how frameworks should wrap Cx:
```rust
// CORRECT: Store reference, delegate
pub struct MyContext<'a> {
    cx: &'a Cx<'a>,
    // custom fields
}

// INCORRECT: Store owned Cx (violates lifetime)
pub struct BadContext {
    cx: Cx<'static>,  // ❌ Cannot own Cx
}
```

### 5. Thread Safety
- Document Send/Sync bounds
- Cx is !Send (pinned to region)
- CxRef may be Send if needed

## Non-Goals
- Changing Cx implementation (just exposure)
- Adding fastapi-specific methods to Cx
- Breaking existing Cx users

## Testing
- [ ] Compile test: external crate can import and use Cx
- [ ] Doc tests: all examples compile and run
- [ ] Integration test: wrap Cx in custom context type

