## Overview

Define the native AsupersyncService trait that integrates with the Cx capability context.

## Trait Design

```rust
use crate::cx::Cx;
use std::future::Future;

/// A service that processes requests within an asupersync context.
/// 
/// Unlike Tower's Service trait, AsupersyncService:
/// - Takes a `&Cx` for cancellation, budgets, and capabilities
/// - Is async-native (no poll_ready, no Future associated type)
/// - Supports the four-valued Outcome system
/// 
/// # Example
/// ```
/// struct MyService;
/// 
/// impl AsupersyncService<Request> for MyService {
///     type Response = Response;
///     type Error = MyError;
///     
///     async fn call(&self, cx: &Cx, req: Request) -> Result<Response, MyError> {
///         // Service implementation
///         Ok(Response::new())
///     }
/// }
/// ```
#[async_trait]
pub trait AsupersyncService<Request>: Send + Sync {
    /// The response type returned by the service.
    type Response;

    /// The error type returned by the service.
    type Error;

    /// Process a request within the given context.
    /// 
    /// The context provides:
    /// - Cancellation checking (`cx.is_cancelled()`)
    /// - Budget access (`cx.remaining_deadline()`)
    /// - Capability verification
    /// - Structured logging context
    async fn call(&self, cx: &Cx, request: Request) -> Result<Self::Response, Self::Error>;
}
```

