# Task: Update TcpStream split() to Share Registration

## What

Update the split read/write halves of TcpStream to correctly share the reactor registration using Arc.

## Location

`src/net/tcp/split.rs`

## Current Implementation

The split API exists but may not handle Registration correctly with Phase 2.

## New Implementation

```rust
use std::sync::Arc;

/// Read half of a split TcpStream.
pub struct ReadHalf<'a> {
    stream: &'a TcpStream,
}

/// Write half of a split TcpStream.
pub struct WriteHalf<'a> {
    stream: &'a TcpStream,
}

impl TcpStream {
    /// Split the stream into read and write halves (borrowed).
    pub fn split(&mut self) -> (ReadHalf<'_>, WriteHalf<'_>) {
        (ReadHalf { stream: self }, WriteHalf { stream: self })
    }
}

impl AsyncRead for ReadHalf<'_> {
    fn poll_read(self: Pin<&mut Self>, cx: &mut Context<'_>, buf: &mut ReadBuf<'_>) -> Poll<io::Result<()>> {
        // Delegate to underlying stream
        Pin::new(&mut *self.stream).poll_read(cx, buf)
    }
}

impl AsyncWrite for WriteHalf<'_> {
    fn poll_write(self: Pin<&mut Self>, cx: &mut Context<'_>, buf: &[u8]) -> Poll<io::Result<usize>> {
        Pin::new(&mut *self.stream).poll_write(cx, buf)
    }

    fn poll_flush(self: Pin<&mut Self>, cx: &mut Context<'_>) -> Poll<io::Result<()>> {
        Pin::new(&mut *self.stream).poll_flush(cx)
    }

    fn poll_shutdown(self: Pin<&mut Self>, cx: &mut Context<'_>) -> Poll<io::Result<()>> {
        Pin::new(&mut *self.stream).poll_shutdown(cx)
    }
}

// --- Owned split variant ---

/// Owned read half (can be sent to another task).
pub struct OwnedReadHalf {
    inner: Arc<TcpStreamInner>,
}

/// Owned write half (can be sent to another task).
pub struct OwnedWriteHalf {
    inner: Arc<TcpStreamInner>,
    shutdown_on_drop: bool,
}

struct TcpStreamInner {
    stream: net::TcpStream,
    registration: Option<Registration>,
}

impl TcpStream {
    /// Split into owned halves (can be sent to different tasks).
    pub fn into_split(self) -> (OwnedReadHalf, OwnedWriteHalf) {
        let inner = Arc::new(TcpStreamInner {
            stream: self.inner,
            registration: self.registration,
        });

        (
            OwnedReadHalf { inner: Arc::clone(&inner) },
            OwnedWriteHalf { inner, shutdown_on_drop: true },
        )
    }
}

impl AsyncRead for OwnedReadHalf {
    fn poll_read(self: Pin<&mut Self>, cx: &mut Context<'_>, buf: &mut ReadBuf<'_>) -> Poll<io::Result<()>> {
        match (&self.inner.stream).read(buf.unfilled()) {
            Ok(n) => { buf.advance(n); Poll::Ready(Ok(())) }
            Err(ref e) if e.kind() == io::ErrorKind::WouldBlock => Poll::Pending,
            Err(e) => Poll::Ready(Err(e)),
        }
    }
}

// Similar for OwnedWriteHalf...

impl OwnedReadHalf {
    /// Reunite with write half to get back TcpStream.
    pub fn reunite(self, write: OwnedWriteHalf) -> Result<TcpStream, ReuniteError> {
        if Arc::ptr_eq(&self.inner, &write.inner) {
            // Prevent shutdown on drop since we're reuniting
            std::mem::forget(write);

            let inner = Arc::try_unwrap(self.inner)
                .map_err(|_| ReuniteError)?;

            Ok(TcpStream {
                inner: inner.stream,
                registration: inner.registration,
            })
        } else {
            Err(ReuniteError)
        }
    }
}
```

## Registration Sharing Strategy

The Registration is shared via Arc<TcpStreamInner>:
- Both halves reference the same Registration
- Registration lives until both halves dropped
- No double-deregistration (single Arc)

## Thread Safety

- `Registration` is `!Send` + `!Sync` (thread-local reactor)
- `OwnedReadHalf` and `OwnedWriteHalf` can be sent to same task, not different threads
- For multi-threaded, need thread-safe Registration (future work)

