# RaptorQ Decoding Pipeline

## Overview
Implements the core RaptorQ fountain code decoding pipeline that reconstructs original data from a set of received symbols, tolerating symbol loss and corruption.

## Technical Background

RaptorQ decoding reconstructs K source symbols from:
- Any K' symbols where K' is slightly larger than K (typically K' = K * 1.01 + 2)
- Mix of source and repair symbols
- Symbols can arrive out of order

The key insight: decode succeeds probabilistically once threshold is met.

## Architecture

```
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|                    DecodingPipeline                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|  Input: Stream of (SymbolId, Symbol) pairs                |
|                  |                                         |
|  +-----------------------------------+                     |
|  | 1. Symbol Collection              |                     |
|  |    - Track received symbols       |                     |
|  |    - Deduplicate by SymbolId      |                     |
|  |    - Group by Source Block Number |                     |
|  +-----------------------------------+                     |
|                  |                                         |
|  +-----------------------------------+                     |
|  | 2. Threshold Detection            |                     |
|  |    - Monitor per-block counts     |                     |
|  |    - Trigger decode at K'         |                     |
|  +-----------------------------------+                     |
|                  |                                         |
|  +-----------------------------------+                     |
|  | 3. Matrix Inversion               |                     |
|  |    - Build encoding matrix        |                     |
|  |    - Gaussian elimination         |                     |
|  |    - Back-substitution            |                     |
|  +-----------------------------------+                     |
|                  |                                         |
|  +-----------------------------------+                     |
|  | 4. Source Symbol Recovery         |                     |
|  |    - Compute intermediate symbols |                     |
|  |    - Generate missing source      |                     |
|  |    - Verify via authentication    |                     |
|  +-----------------------------------+                     |
|                  |                                         |
|  Output: Result<Vec<u8>, DecodingError>                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
```

## Core Types

```rust
/// The main decoding pipeline
pub struct DecodingPipeline {
    config: DecodingConfig,
    blocks: HashMap<u8, BlockDecoder>,
    completed_blocks: BTreeSet<u8>,
    auth_context: Option<SecurityContext>,
}

/// Configuration for decoding
#[derive(Debug, Clone)]
pub struct DecodingConfig {
    /// Expected symbol size (must match encoding)
    pub symbol_size: u16,
    /// Maximum symbols to buffer per block
    pub max_buffered_symbols: usize,
    /// Decoding timeout per block
    pub block_timeout: Duration,
    /// Whether to verify authentication tags
    pub verify_auth: bool,
}

/// Per-block decoder state
struct BlockDecoder {
    sbn: u8,
    received: SymbolSet,
    k: Option<u16>,  // Learned from first source symbol or metadata
    state: BlockDecodingState,
}

enum BlockDecodingState {
    Collecting,
    Decoding,
    Decoded(Vec<Symbol>),
    Failed(DecodingError),
}

/// Result of feeding a symbol
pub enum SymbolAcceptResult {
    /// Symbol accepted, still collecting
    Accepted { received: usize, needed: usize },
    /// Threshold reached, decoding started
    DecodingStarted { block_sbn: u8 },
    /// Block fully decoded
    BlockComplete { block_sbn: u8, data: Vec<u8> },
    /// Duplicate symbol ignored
    Duplicate,
    /// Symbol rejected (wrong object, corrupt, etc.)
    Rejected(RejectReason),
}
```

