## Recovery Strategies

### 1. Partial Block Decoding
- Attempt decode when K' symbols received
- If fails, continue collecting more repair symbols
- Retry with each new symbol until success or timeout

### 2. Block Independence
- Each source block decodes independently
- Partial success possible (some blocks decoded, others pending)
- Application can use partially decoded data

### 3. Symbol Prioritization
- Source symbols preferred (no computation needed)
- Low-ESI repair symbols preferred (simpler encoding)

## Integration with Transport

```rust
async fn receive_object(stream: SymbolStream, ctx: SecurityContext) -> Result<Vec<u8>, Error> {
    let mut decoder = DecodingPipeline::with_auth(config, ctx);

    while let Some(symbol) = stream.next().await {
        match decoder.feed(symbol)? {
            SymbolAcceptResult::BlockComplete { .. } => {
                tracing::info!("Block decoded");
            }
            SymbolAcceptResult::Accepted { received, needed } => {
                tracing::debug!(received, needed, "Symbol accepted");
            }
            _ => {}
        }

        if decoder.is_complete() {
            break;
        }
    }

    decoder.into_data()
}
```

