# Task: Implement EpollReactor::register with EPOLLET

## What

Implement the register() method for EpollReactor using edge-triggered mode.

## Location

`src/runtime/reactor/epoll.rs`

## Design

```rust
impl Reactor for EpollReactor {
    fn register(
        &self,
        source: &dyn Source,
        interest: Interest,
        waker: Waker,
    ) -> io::Result<Registration> {
        let fd = source.raw_fd();

        let mut inner = self.inner.lock().unwrap();

        // Allocate token and store waker
        let token = inner.wakers.insert(waker);
        inner.fds.insert(token, fd);

        // Build epoll event
        let mut event = EpollEvent::new(
            self.interest_to_epoll_flags(interest) | EpollFlags::EPOLLET,
            token.to_usize() as u64,
        );

        // Add to epoll
        epoll_ctl(self.epoll_fd, EpollOp::EpollCtlAdd, fd, Some(&mut event))
            .map_err(|e| {
                // Cleanup on failure
                inner.wakers.remove(token);
                inner.fds.remove(&token);
                io::Error::from_raw_os_error(e as i32)
            })?;

        // Create Registration with weak ref to self
        Ok(Registration::new(
            token,
            Arc::downgrade(&/* self as Arc */),
            interest,
        ))
    }
}

impl EpollReactor {
    fn interest_to_epoll_flags(&self, interest: Interest) -> EpollFlags {
        let mut flags = EpollFlags::empty();
        if interest.contains(Interest::READABLE) {
            flags |= EpollFlags::EPOLLIN;
        }
        if interest.contains(Interest::WRITABLE) {
            flags |= EpollFlags::EPOLLOUT;
        }
        // Note: EPOLLERR and EPOLLHUP are always reported
        flags
    }
}
```

## Edge-Triggered Semantics (EPOLLET)

With EPOLLET:
1. Event fires when state *changes* (not while condition persists)
2. Must read/write until EAGAIN before next event
3. More efficient but requires careful application code

## Error Handling

| Error | Cause | Action |
|-------|-------|--------|
| EBADF | Invalid fd | Return error |
| EEXIST | Already registered | Return error (caller bug) |
| ENOMEM | Kernel limit | Return error |
| ENOSPC | /proc/sys/fs/epoll/max_user_watches | Return error |

