# Task: Implement LabReactor with Virtual Event Queue

## What

Create the LabReactor that maintains a queue of scheduled I/O events and delivers them based on virtual time.

## Location

`src/runtime/reactor/lab.rs` (new file)
`src/lab/reactor.rs` (alternative, if keeping lab separate)

## Design

```rust
use std::cell::RefCell;
use std::collections::{BinaryHeap, VecDeque};
use std::rc::Rc;

/// Simulated reactor for deterministic testing.
///
/// No real I/O operations - events are scheduled and delivered
/// based on virtual time progression.
pub struct LabReactor {
    /// Min-heap of scheduled events, ordered by delivery time
    scheduled: RefCell<BinaryHeap<ScheduledEvent>>,
    /// Events ready for immediate delivery
    ready: RefCell<VecDeque<Event>>,
    /// Token → Waker mapping
    wakers: RefCell<TokenSlab>,
    /// Token → Source metadata
    sources: RefCell<HashMap<Token, LabSource>>,
    /// Virtual time reference (shared with LabRuntime)
    time: Rc<RefCell<Time>>,
    /// Trace buffer (shared)
    trace: Rc<RefCell<TraceBuffer>>,
    /// Wake flag for simulated wakeup
    wake_flag: Cell<bool>,
    /// Config
    config: LabReactorConfig,
    /// RNG for controlled randomness
    rng: RefCell<StdRng>,
}

#[derive(Eq, PartialEq)]
struct ScheduledEvent {
    deliver_at: Time,
    token: Token,
    ready: Interest,
    sequence: u64, // For deterministic ordering of same-time events
}

impl Ord for ScheduledEvent {
    fn cmp(&self, other: &Self) -> Ordering {
        // Min-heap: earlier time = higher priority
        other.deliver_at.cmp(&self.deliver_at)
            .then_with(|| other.sequence.cmp(&self.sequence))
    }
}

struct LabSource {
    /// Simulated current readiness state
    readiness: Interest,
    /// Interest being monitored
    interest: Interest,
    /// Associated waker
    waker: Waker,
}

pub struct LabReactorConfig {
    /// Default latency for I/O operations (0 = instant)
    pub io_latency: Duration,
    /// Seed for RNG
    pub seed: u64,
}

impl LabReactor {
    pub fn new(time: Rc<RefCell<Time>>, config: LabReactorConfig) -> Self {
        Self {
            scheduled: RefCell::new(BinaryHeap::new()),
            ready: RefCell::new(VecDeque::new()),
            wakers: RefCell::new(TokenSlab::new()),
            sources: RefCell::new(HashMap::new()),
            time,
            trace: Rc::new(RefCell::new(TraceBuffer::new())),
            wake_flag: Cell::new(false),
            config,
            rng: RefCell::new(StdRng::seed_from_u64(config.seed)),
        }
    }

    /// Schedule an event for future delivery (test API).
    pub fn schedule_event(&self, token: Token, ready: Interest, delay: Duration) {
        let deliver_at = *self.time.borrow() + delay;
        let sequence = self.next_sequence();
        self.scheduled.borrow_mut().push(ScheduledEvent {
            deliver_at,
            token,
            ready,
            sequence,
        });
    }

    /// Make a source immediately readable/writable (test API).
    pub fn set_ready(&self, token: Token, ready: Interest) {
        self.ready.borrow_mut().push_back(Event { token, ready });
    }

    /// Advance time and deliver due events (called by LabRuntime).
    pub fn advance_time_to(&self, target: Time) {
        let mut scheduled = self.scheduled.borrow_mut();
        let mut ready = self.ready.borrow_mut();

        while let Some(event) = scheduled.peek() {
            if event.deliver_at <= target {
                let event = scheduled.pop().unwrap();
                ready.push_back(Event {
                    token: event.token,
                    ready: event.ready,
                });
            } else {
                break;
            }
        }
    }
}
```

## Virtual Time Integration

The LabReactor doesn't own time - it receives it from LabRuntime:

```rust
// In LabRuntime::advance_time()
pub fn advance_time(&self, delta: Duration) {
    let new_time = self.time.borrow() + delta;
    *self.time.borrow_mut() = new_time;

    // Tell reactor to deliver due events
    if let Some(reactor) = &self.reactor {
        reactor.advance_time_to(new_time);
    }
}
```

